If you need both a logo and a website, getting them designed together — rather than separately — has real advantages. Here's why it's worth considering.

## Visual consistency from the start

When a website is designed around a logo that already exists, the designer adapts to fit. When both are designed together, everything is built as a unified identity: logo colours inform the website palette, typographic choices carry through from the logo to headings and body text, and the overall aesthetic is cohesive rather than assembled from separate parts.

The result looks more intentional and more professional — because it is.

## Fewer revisions, faster delivery

Separate projects often create back-and-forth. A website is built, then the logo changes slightly, which requires updates to the website. Or the website design reveals that certain colours don't work together, requiring revisions to the brand identity.

When both are running in the same project with the same designer, these issues surface and get resolved earlier — and the overall process moves faster.

## Cost efficiency

At NC Digital, clients having both a logo and a website designed together get the logo at a reduced price. The workflow is more efficient for both sides, and the saving is passed on.

## A complete starting point

For new businesses especially, arriving with a logo, a website, and a consistent brand identity means you're ready from day one — rather than piecing things together over time and fixing inconsistencies later.

## How it works

We handle the logo first, typically in the first week of the project. Once the logo direction is confirmed, the website design builds from it. By the time the website is complete, everything is integrated and consistent.

See our [logo design service](/services/logo-design/) and [web design service](/services/web-design/) for details on what's included in each. Or [get in touch](/contact/) to discuss a combined package.
